>1) Why can't I N)ame my blessed +1 long sword Excalibur? Every 
>time I try, my hand slips and I screw up one random letter. (My 
>dex is 18 and I'm wearing +0 leather gloves.) I assume this is 
>a pretty common problem with an easy solution.

  Special artifacts are not to be obtained merely by engraving a
name.  All are given to you by your god, with the exception of
Excalibur, which is a gift of the lady of the lake (or, well, the
lady of the fountain, I guess).  

>2) How do you create dragon scale mail from a corpse? I've
>tried #offering dead dragons but they're consumed like anything else.
>Also, why is grey dragon scale mail better than other armors
>(like crystal plate mail, for example)?

  Gray (note spelling) dragon scale mail gives magic protection, just
like a cloak of magic protection, and frees you to wear some other
kind of cloak.  Without magic protection you will not long survive in
the depths of hell.
  Do you know that when you polymorph an alligator corpse, it turns
into a pair of shoes?

>3) Does Stormbringer have any special properties besides barely ever
>missing an opponent? I seem to regenerate quickly, but I can't be
>sure if this is related to the sword. I know the fictional version
>of the sword had a similar power.
>
  Well, you have probably noticed that Stormy gives a different
message than other weapons.  If you want to see exactly what it
means, try using a stethoscope on the monster you're fighting,
and watch what happens to it.  Exercise:  think about possible
applications to the Wizard of Yendor.
  It doesn't help you regenerate faster, this happens automatically
as you gain levels.

>4) Is it legal (possible) to use a wand of wishing to wish for a
>scroll of recharging, and then recharge the wand when it runs out
>of wishes? 
>
  Try it and see.

>5) How can I create holy water from my potions of water? Is unholy
>water benificial for a chaotic character?

  With most items, dropping them on altars tells you whether they are
blessed or cursed.  Not so with water.  Try it.  Try dipping things
in the various kinds of water, and see what happens.

